From 71482e5392bac5a02a7cde5fdebaa93b9182d118 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:02:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: add a dB volume control mirrored into
 MSPP

On Windows the speaker graph runs VOL_CTRL ahead of the MSPP
post-processing module, and each volume change sets the VOL_CTRL gain
and sends the same gain to MSPP as PARAM_ID_MSPP_VOLUME, which MSPP's
tuning depends on.

Add a topology control type, SND_SOC_AR_TPLG_VOL_DB_CTL, for the
VOL_CTRL widget: -79..0 dB in 0.5 dB steps, -14.5 dB default, with the
range and TLV enforced so userspace can use it as a hardware volume.

A live write goes to VOL_CTRL and then to every MSPP of the graph and
is only confirmed once all took it; otherwise the confirmed step is
restored, then VOL_CTRL is muted, and if even that fails the graph is
torn down with the new q6apm_graph_fault() so it never plays at
mismatched gains. Prepare and POST_PMU replay the confirmed step. A
graph with MSPP may hold only one such control, and MSPP_VOLUME is not
sent unless the DSP echoes whole tokens.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
